# Generated output — never formatted, never linted.
dist/
coverage/
node_modules/
.venv/

# Lockfiles are tool-owned; formatting them would fight the tool.
# image-lock.yaml is validated against a strict canonical grammar by
# scripts/check-images.mjs — a second formatter would be a second grammar.
pnpm-lock.yaml
uv.lock
deploy/images/image-lock.yaml

# Python is formatted by ruff, not Prettier. Two formatters over one file is
# the exact conflict the single-authority rule exists to prevent.
*.py

# Markdown is prose. Prettier reflows it in ways that fight hand-wrapped
# documentation and Mermaid blocks, so it is left alone deliberately.
*.md

# Lint FIXTURES are deliberately invalid: their whole purpose is to make a rule
# or the parser fire. Formatting them would repair the very violations they
# exist to prove are caught -- which it did once, silently, before this entry.
packages/lint-config/tests/fixtures/
